# next-pwa build artifacts -- fully generated at build time, must not be
# committed. public/sw.js is back in this list as of S1141 (2026-07-20):
# it was previously hand-written (Feature #69) with a carve-out removing it
# from this ignore list, but that hand-written version was silently
# overwritten by every real build anyway (no swSrc/customWorkerDir was
# configured, so next-pwa's GenerateSW always regenerates it from scratch).
# The real, build-surviving source of custom SW logic is now
# packages/frontend/worker/index.js (see next.config.js's customWorkerDir),
# which next-pwa bundles into public/worker-*.js and auto-merges into this
# generated sw.js. public/sw-cache.js and public/sw-push.js below are
# pre-existing untracked local files (confirmed via git ls-files -- never
# actually committed) from an earlier, never-wired-up attempt at the same
# thing; their real logic has been ported into worker/index.js.
public/sw.js
public/sw-cache.js
public/sw-push.js
public/worker-*.js
public/workbox-*.js
public/fallback-*.js
